{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A perfect lamb.</b> That it be without blemish. Also, \"lamb\" is a general term for each of the two species that the term flock includes — thus \"lamb of sheep and lamb of goats\" (Deuteronomy 14:4). R. Moses ben Amram the Persian said: the lamb is an obligation for the Passover of Egypt, but in the land of Israel, a lamb or an ox. His proof: \"And you shall slaughter a Passover to YHWH your Elohim, flock and herd\" (Deuteronomy 16:2) — which is the Passover of generations. But this is not correct, for every Passover of generations is a remembrance of the Passover of Egypt, and it is not fitting to change. Rather, \"and you shall slaughter a Passover to YHWH your Elohim, flock\" is the obligation, and \"herd\" for peace-offerings, to eat during the festival boiled in water and similar. Likewise, \"and you shall rejoice in your festival, you and your son and your daughter\" (Deuteronomy 16:14): you are obligated; your son and your daughter are optional. And the proof is that it is written in Chronicles that they slaughtered on the fourteenth day lambs and oxen, and there it is written: the lambs for Passover-offerings and the oxen for peace-offerings; they boiled them in pots and caldrons, but only the flock they boiled in fire, as required. R. Yeshua said: there is a difference between \"a year old\" and \"in its year\": \"a year old\" — a full year has passed for it; \"in its year\" — as it sounds. Now in the offering of the princes: \"one lamb in its year\" (Numbers 7:21), and afterward it is written: \"lambs a year old\" (Numbers 7:23)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "שב שם יד likely a corruption or abbreviation for שם שם י\"ד ('there, there 14'); resolved to Deuteronomy 16:14 based on the verse quoted. The phrase בשלו אותם בדודים ובסירות רק לבד הצאן בשלו באש כמשפט refers to II Chronicles 35:13."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:31.889771654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}